// Your routes of land and static art: which land source and which land id draws a land id, and which item art a
// static draws. Dynamapper reads your copy, cache/runtime_specs/land/LandRoutes.kdl beside the assets folder, in place
// of this file when it exists: copy this file there and edit the copy. Saving the copy applies it to the open map; a
// copy that does not read leaves this file in force, with a warning naming the line, until it is fixed.
//
// The `routes` block always applies. A `profile` applies on top of it while it is chosen as the "Season / profile"
// in Preferences > Graphics; a profile's route of an id replaces the `routes` block's. The profiles below are the
// Classic client's seasons.
//
//   land <id> [<last id>] [source="cc"|"ec"|"kr"] [id=<land id>|terrain=<terrain definition>]
//     Draws the land id, or every id from <id> to <last id>, from the source (Classic, Enhanced or Kingdom Reborn;
//     the Land Texture Source preference when left out) as the land id `id` of that source (the same id when left
//     out). `terrain` names an Enhanced or Kingdom Reborn terrain definition (TerrainDefinition id) instead: the
//     first land id of that source drawn with it.
//   item <id> [<last id>] id=<item id>
//     Statics of the item id, or of every id up to <last id>, draw the item `id` with its tile data, as the Classic
//     client does for its seasons. Multis are not routed.
//   when player-x-below=<x> [map=<map>]
//     In a profile only: the profile applies only while the player's x is below <x>, on the map <map>, or on every
//     map when left out. On each map the `when` naming it decides, else the one without `map`; a profile with `when`
//     nodes, none of which covers the map, does not apply there. A profile without `when` applies everywhere. The
//     player crossing the line switches the profile on or off at once.
//
// An id is routed once per block. A route whose source lacks the id it names falls back to the usual chain (the
// selected source, the other Enhanced-layout source, then Classic), with a warning; Classic selected never draws
// Enhanced-layout land, so its routes to "ec" or "kr" are skipped, with a warning.
//
// routes {
//     land 0x0003 source="ec" id=0x0004    // land 3 drawn as the Enhanced land 4
//     land 0x0010 0x0015 source="cc"       // land 0x10 to 0x15, each as itself, from Classic
//     land 0x0020 source="kr" terrain=12   // the Kingdom Reborn terrain definition 12
//     item 0x0CCA id=0x0CCB                // statics 0xCCA draw the item 0xCCB
// }

routes {
}

